course: dictionary
lesson: 3495
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word farm can be a noun or a verb, and the meaning changes with the job it does. As a noun, a farm is a place: land with buildings where people grow crops and keep animals. «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» The gates belong to a place, so farm names the place.
explain: As a verb, farm is an action: to farm means to grow crops or keep animals for food. To check which one you have, ask whether the word names a thing or does a job. If you can put «a» or «the» in front of it, it is probably a noun. If you can put «to» in front of it, it is probably a verb.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «People in the Andes tamed guinea pigs thousands of years ago and kept them as farm animals.» Here farm animals means animals that live on a farm. Context tells you which meaning is right, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A farm is land with buildings where people grow crops and keep animals.
fact: To farm means to grow crops or keep animals for food.
fact: Some farms raise fish, and a fish farm is a farm for fish.
fact: «Farming began only about 12,000 years ago», and people like us had lived for about 300,000 years before that.
fact: «Wheeled carts appeared about 5,500 years ago», long after farming and pottery had begun.
exercise: «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» What is a farm in this sentence? | A long walk to the shops | A kind of gate that opens by itself | *A place with land and buildings where animals are kept | A type of animal
exercise: Mia says, «We farm sheep on the hill.» What does farm mean here? | To sell tickets at a fair | *To keep animals and grow things for food | To run very fast up a hill | To dig holes in the ground
exercise: Which sentence uses farm as a noun? | We farm turnips every year | The farmers farm every single day | *Our farm has cows, hens and a big red barn | Dad will farm the land next spring
test: Which phrase names a fish farm? | Fishing boat out at sea | *A place where fish are raised for food | A river where fish swim freely | A fish and chip shop
test: Grandma says, «Guinea pigs were farmed in the Andes long ago.» What does farmed mean? | Carried them in a cart over the hills | Painted pictures of animals | Lost them in the mountains | *Kept animals for food, as farm animals
exam: Which sentence uses farm as a verb? | *We farm wheat and keep hens on our land | The farm gate was open all day | Farm animals need plenty of food | Our farm is by the river
